// Coroutine integration test
//
// The codegen marks ANY function containing `yield` as a generator
// (SET_FUNC_GENERATOR).  Calling a generator-flagged function via
// the CALL opcode just creates a GeneratorObject without executing
// the body.  To bypass this, we use kern_start_coroutine(), which
// creates a Coroutine entry directly so the resumeAll() loop in
// the host picks it up.
//
// Expected output (VM::run() executes the main script first, then
// resumeAll() runs the coroutine body through each yield):
//   OK: test_coroutines
//   a
//   b
//   c

def task() {
    print("a")
    yield
    print("b")
    yield
    print("c")
}

// Start task as a cooperative coroutine (returns coroutine ID).
// The host's runSource() calls resumeAll() in a loop after run(),
// which restores and runs the coroutine until each yield.
kern_start_coroutine(task, [])

print("OK: test_coroutines")
